TODO: Keeping file and folder names in line with your naming format. Starts by answering whether Radarr and Sonarr already do this: they rename only on import or when you run it by hand, so names go stale. This matters most for TV, where episodes imported as TBA, changed TMDB IDs, and out-of-date years leave names that Plex and Jellyfin can't match. Makes clear that Profilarr never renames anything itself: it tells the Arr to rename, which is why Profilarr doesn't need access to your library files. Covers what a rename run checks, renaming folders, skipping items with an ignore tag, dry runs and their limits, scheduling, and summary or detailed notifications.
